<!--
  ============================================================================
  RM_GreySeaSessile.xml               TerminalBiomes · authored 2026-09-26
  ============================================================================
  GREYSEA_SESSILE_LAYER_1 — the small abundant layer at the base of the Grey
  Sea floor's food chain.

  Owner, 2026-09-26, verbatim, one sentence:
      "Abundant shrimp, clam and mussel equivalents lurk among the
       formations, picking through what organic matter rains down from the
       surface."

  ============================================================================
  🔴 ALL THREE ARE NEW — and that OVERRODE the capture's own position
  ============================================================================
  RULED at the bench 2026-09-26 (content doc Q5, sheet §4): a shrimp, a clam
  AND a mussel, all new defs. BENCH had positioned that RM_Fessk already
  covers "shrimp" and only two new sessile defs were owed; the owner ruled
  otherwise and added the third.

  ⇒ The constraint that came with it: **the new shrimp must be SMALL and
  must never read as a second ossuary shrimp.** RM_Fessk is man-sized
  (baseBodySize 0.9), intelligent, evasive, watching from behind a pillar,
  and the sheet's line about it is "The shrimp saw you first." RM_Nissik
  below is baseBodySize 0.08 — a hand-sized picker in the litter that
  nothing watches and nothing fears. Two animals, one word, no overlap.

  ============================================================================
  "ABUNDANT" DOES NOT CROSS BAN 2 — and here is exactly how
  ============================================================================
  the_grey_deep.md §6 ban 2 and terminator_sea.md §6: "no herds, flocks,
  schools, packs or swarms … fauna are single-spawn and low-density by def."
  RULED ADDITIVE 2026-09-26: abundance here is MANY INDIVIDUAL SPAWNS of
  slow or sessile things at moderate commonality — "a cluster on a mussel
  pillar is a placement, not a moving group."

  In engine terms, and this is the whole of the compliance:
    - commonality carries the abundance (0.7-0.9, the highest on this sea),
    - wildGroupSize stays at or near 1, so nothing spawns as a party,
    - MoveSpeed is 0.4-1.2, so nothing MOVES as a group even by accident.
  ⛔ Never raise wildGroupSize here to "make them abundant". That is the
  exact thing the ban forbids, and commonality is the field that does the
  job legally.

  ============================================================================
  EQUIVALENTS, NEVER EARTH ANIMALS
  ============================================================================
  Ban 6 and the standing recognisability ban. "Shrimp/clam/mussel" are the
  owner's shorthand for a NICHE, not a species list: none of the three below
  is named, described or shaped as its Earth counterpart, and none may be
  retitled to one. The names are invented exotic words, which per the
  project's Q11a rule are NOT franchise IP and therefore ship RM_-tier,
  cast inline on RM_GreySea with no MayRequire.

  ============================================================================
  TWO DEFS EACH — floor resident AND catch
  ============================================================================
  Standing sea law, restated by the owner 2026-09-26: "All the fishables
  should also be alive and moving around in the depths (this is true for ALL
  seas)." These three are catchable, so each owes a *Catch item
  (RM_GreySeaSessileCatch.xml) and a fishTypes row. The shipped precedent is
  RM_Essarn <-> RM_EssarnCatch.

  They are also the Brine Crown's prey — his own spec for that plant names
  "small bottom-dwelling grazers" getting impaled, and this file is who those
  are.

  PLACEHOLDER ART: flat texPaths under Things/Pawn/Animal/<defName>/, the
  same posture RM_GreySeaFauna.xml already established for the five shipped
  Grey residents. Real art is owed via artpipe; search done/ and _artsrc/ by
  subject before queuing anything.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       RM_NISSIK — the shrimp equivalent. SMALL, and authored against
       the risk of reading as a second RM_Fessk.
       ================================================================== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Nissik</defName>
    <label>nissik</label>
    <description>A hand-sized, glass-bodied picker that works the litter at the foot of the formations, going over the same square of sediment again and again for whatever has settled out of the water since the last pass. Everything it eats fell from somewhere above. There is no shortage of them and there never has been; a diver's lamp turns up forty in a stride, all of them busy, none of them interested.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>1.2</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>3</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>55</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <Wildness>0.75</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>pick</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>1</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.5</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>Snake</body>
      <baseBodySize>0.08</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.2</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.15</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>OmnivoreAnimal</foodType>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <lifeExpectancy>3</lifeExpectancy>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.08</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.15</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalCommon</li>
    </tradeTags>
    <modExtensions>
      <!-- GREYSEA_LAMP_RESPONSE_BUILD_1 layer 1: drawn to a player light on the Grey (RM_BaskInGlow) -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.TerminalBiomes.RM_SeekGlowExtension">
        <mode>drawn</mode>
        <gate>greyDrawn</gate>
        <onlyBiome>RM_GreySea</onlyBiome>
        <seekChancePerCheck>0.15</seekChancePerCheck>
        <minGlowRadiusToTarget>1.5</minGlowRadiusToTarget>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Nissik</defName>
    <label>nissik</label>
    <race>RM_Nissik</race>
    <combatPower>3</combatPower>
    <!-- Single-spawn. The abundance is commonality 0.9 on the biome. -->
    <wildGroupSize>1</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.04</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Nissik/RM_Nissik</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.16</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Nissik/RM_Nissik</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.22</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Nissik/RM_Nissik</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.3</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       RM_THOLLIM — the clam equivalent. "The clam sits in sediment"
       (sheet §4). Effectively immobile: MoveSpeed 0.4 rather than 0,
       because a RimWorld Pawn with no movement at all cannot satisfy
       its own job graph and reads as a bug in the log rather than as a
       clam.
       ================================================================== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Thollim</defName>
    <label>thollim</label>
    <description>A pair of thick grey valves sitting half down in the sediment with a finger's width of gape, taking in whatever the water brings and putting out nothing anyone has noticed. It moves about the length of itself in a season, and only downward. Prise one up and the inside is a knot of dense pale meat that keeps for a fortnight in its own brine — which is why every shore camp on this sea has a heap of shells behind it.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>0.4</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>7</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>55</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <Wildness>0.3</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>shell</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>2</power>
        <cooldownTime>3</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>Snake</body>
      <baseBodySize>0.2</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.6</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.1</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>VegetarianRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <lifeExpectancy>25</lifeExpectancy>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.3</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.8</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalCommon</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Thollim</defName>
    <label>thollim</label>
    <race>RM_Thollim</race>
    <combatPower>4</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>1</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.06</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Thollim/RM_Thollim</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.2</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Thollim/RM_Thollim</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.3</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Thollim/RM_Thollim</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.4</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       RM_GRUSK — the mussel equivalent. "The mussel clusters on pillars
       and domes" (sheet §4).

       ⚠️ wildGroupSize 1~4 is the ONE place in this file where a number
       above 1 appears, and it is the placement the sheet explicitly
       permits: "a cluster on a pillar is a placement, not a moving
       group." At MoveSpeed 0.5 a grusk cannot form a moving group, so
       the ban's object — herds, flocks, schools, packs, swarms — cannot
       arise from this value. The shipped precedent for a clustered
       slow shelled thing on this sea is RM_Sorruth's own 1~3.
       ================================================================== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Grusk</defName>
    <label>grusk</label>
    <description>A wedge of blue-black shell cemented to the side of a pillar by a mineral foot it grows and cannot ungrow, filtering the water that runs past the column. Where there is one there are usually a dozen along the same face, all pointing the same way into the current, none of them within reach of another. Under the shell there is a thumb of dark meat that tastes strongly of the sea's own chemistry, and shore-folk argue about whether that is a recommendation.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>0.5</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>6</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>55</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <Wildness>0.3</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>shell</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>2</power>
        <cooldownTime>3</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>Snake</body>
      <baseBodySize>0.12</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.45</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.1</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>VegetarianRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <lifeExpectancy>15</lifeExpectancy>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.2</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.5</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalCommon</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Grusk</defName>
    <label>grusk</label>
    <race>RM_Grusk</race>
    <combatPower>3</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>1~4</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.05</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Grusk/RM_Grusk</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.18</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Grusk/RM_Grusk</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.25</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Grusk/RM_Grusk</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.34</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
